@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
### Register a student
# @name registerStudent
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Student One",
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "password": "pass123",
  "role": "student"
}

### Register a teacher
# @name registerTeacher
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Teacher One",
  "email": "teacher@example.com",
  "password": "pass123",
  "role": "teacher"
}

### Login as student
# @name loginStudent
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### Login as teacher
# @name loginTeacher
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "teacher@example.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}
###
# @name startAttempt
POST {{baseUrl}}/quizzes/b5e809c8-c40e-4455-b499-31f07a819572/attempts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStudent.response.body.$.token}}

### Student tries to create a quiz — should be 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/quizzes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStudent.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should Fail",
  "description": "student cannot create this",
  "duration_minutes": 10
}

### Teacher creates a quiz — should succeed
POST {{baseUrl}}/quizzes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTeacher.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Teacher Quiz",
  "description": "teacher can create this",
  "duration_minutes": 10
}

### TEST A - no role field at all (should default to student)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test No Role",
  "email": "noroleuser1@example.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### Empty title — should be 400 with clear message
POST {{baseUrl}}/quizzes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTeacher.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "test",
  "duration_minutes": 10
}

### Negative duration — should be 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/quizzes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTeacher.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Valid Title",
  "description": "test",
  "duration_minutes": -5
}

### Invalid email — should be 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "pass12345"
}

### Short password — should be 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Short Pass",
  "email": "shortpass@example.com",
  "password": "abc"
}
### Submit it
POST {{baseUrl}}/attempts/{{startAttempt.response.body.$.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStudent.response.body.$.token}}

### Now view it — reuse the same captured id
GET {{baseUrl}}/attempts/{{startAttempt.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStudent.response.body.$.token}}

### Student views their own attempt history
GET {{baseUrl}}/my-attempts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStudent.response.body.$.token}}

### Teacher (owner) views attempts for their quiz — should succeed, with student info
GET {{baseUrl}}/quizzes/{b5e809c8-c40e-4455-b499-31f07a819572}/attempts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTeacher.response.body.$.token}}

### A student tries the teacher endpoint — should be 403 (wrong role)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quizzes/{b5e809c8-c40e-4455-b499-31f07a819572}/attempts
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStudent.response.body.$.token}}

### Quiz not found — should be 404 with structured error
GET {{baseUrl}}/quizzes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTeacher.response.body.$.token}}

### Duplicate email — should be 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dup",
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "password": "pass12345"
}

### Empty title — should be 400 with VALIDATION_ERROR code
POST {{baseUrl}}/quizzes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTeacher.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "test",
  "duration_minutes": 10
}